      "text": "To find Bob's favorite number, we need to follow the given conditions step by step:\n\n1. **Identify multiples of 11 between 50 and 100:**\n   The multiples of 11 in this range are:\n   \\[\n   55, 66, 77, 88, 99\n   \\]\n\n2. **Exclude multiples that are also multiples of 2:**\n   From the list above, we identify the multiples of 2:\n   \\[\n   66, 88\n   \\]\n   Removing these, we are left with:\n   \\[\n   55, 77, 99\n   \\]\n\n3. **Check the sum of the digits for each remaining number:**\n   - For \\(55\\):\n     \\[\n     5 + 5 = 10 \\quad (\\text{not a multiple of 3})\n     \\]\n   - For \\(77\\):\n     \\[\n     7 + 7 = 14 \\quad (\\text{not a multiple of 3})\n     \\]\n   - For \\(99\\):\n     \\[\n     9 + 9 = 18 \\quad (\\text{a multiple of 3})\n     \\]\n\n4. **Identify the number that meets all the conditions:**\n   - It is a multiple of 11, but not a multiple of 2.\n   - The sum of its digits is a multiple of 3.\n\n   From our list, the only number that satisfies all these conditions is \\(99\\).\n\nTherefore, Bob's favorite number is \\(\\boxed{99}\\).",
